<p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3f8f4bf7-f6bd-f2dc-1938-1699c2483fe2" id="_3f8f4bf7-f6bd-f2dc-1938-1699c2483fe2"></a><u>Remarks:</u></p>

<p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3318b726-c0a3-94a4-654c-3d94a9b62565" id="_3318b726-c0a3-94a4-654c-3d94a9b62565"></a>The term METAREA followed by a roman numeral and the extensions to uniquely identify a sub area, such as METAREA VIII(N) and METAREA VIII(S), is to be coded by using the  <b>Feature Name</b> attribute. Only the roman number is to be coded in the  <b>Id METAREA</b> attribute. The METAREA coordinator should be encoded as an associated  <b>Authority</b>. The coordinating authority to be associated should be the issuing authority, not the preparation authority, of the METAREA.</p>

