<p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:auto" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_979c6fd6-4fab-8419-f2d5-1bdcdf521e24" id="_979c6fd6-4fab-8419-f2d5-1bdcdf521e24"></a><u>Remarks:</u></p>

<div class="ul_wrap" style="page-break-after:auto"><p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo18;page-break-after:auto" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst"><a name="_58ca024a-f90b-9366-d652-6c93a1fc5e25" id="_58ca024a-f90b-9366-d652-6c93a1fc5e25"></a>In addition to using the <b>typeOfBroadcastContent</b> attribute, <b>subjectDescription</b> attribute may be used to describe the broadcast content of a specific service.
</p>
<p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo18;page-break-after:auto" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast"><a name="_cc97d557-5793-a8b3-69e5-de6c5144e1d5" id="_cc97d557-5793-a8b3-69e5-de6c5144e1d5"></a>The <b>subjectIndicatorCharacter</b> is for encoding the B<sub>2</sub> technical character used to indicate the subject group of the maritime safety information (MSI) message. B<sub>2</sub> subject indicator character is used by the MSI receiver to identify the different classes of messages (MSC.1/Circ.1403/Rev.2).
</p>
</div>

