<p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_32071645-d5b9-3239-7667-cd15b917d18c" id="_32071645-d5b9-3239-7667-cd15b917d18c"></a><u>Remarks:</u></p>

<p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d3f97a43-8dea-78a4-205f-2f38523a75ee" id="_d3f97a43-8dea-78a4-205f-2f38523a75ee"></a>The GML format implements and uses association classes in accordance with ISO 19136-2. The association class is implemented as an information type instance with information associations to and from the two classes linked by the association, as listed above. A generic inverse association must be used if it is necessary to encode a reverse link to a feature instance.</p>

<p style="text-align: left;page-break-after:avoid" class="MsoNormal"><a name="_f2d8f957-c8ee-58fd-a6cd-5e49a53af7c0" id="_f2d8f957-c8ee-58fd-a6cd-5e49a53af7c0"></a><u>Distinction:</u></p>
